  "what_each_layer_could_reach": "NOT SUBMITTED (b + b2 + c) is 52 to 58 percent of all opportunities at rung 1 against 13 to 17 percent at the base, and SUBMITTED-BUT-LATE (a + a2) is 31 to 35 percent against 25 to 38. So the loss is overwhelmingly a RELEASE decision, not a delivery failure, and a C5 attribution rule (layer 2) is the only thing that reaches it directly. But the cap closes BECAUSE monitor first-token times cross C5's 0.8 s trip, and engine priority (layer 1) acts on exactly that, so layer 1 is upstream of layer 2's symptom: it would shrink a directly and b and b2 indirectly by keeping the cap open. The two are not alternatives on the same quantity",
